  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: c454d2cbd878f6c43a1186adcbc49f01, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The Metropol back room. Cards till dawn. Now home to sleep it off.
    midDaysAnswer: The Metropol shut at curfew. Now it's a basement game by the tram depot.
    finalDaysAnswer: A cellar across the river. Three players, one candle. I folded early.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: The evening train from Kutaisi. First time in your town, officer.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: Loading freighters at the port. Honest work. I quit cards years ago.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: The Metropol. The card room's open again. Full tables all night!
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
    cameraTrigger: 
  - question: Are you experiencing any symptoms?
    earlyDaysAnswer: Sweaty palms, as always. Bad for holding cards, good for bluffing.
    midDaysAnswer: I sleep all afternoon and wake tired. The numbers won't sit still.
    finalDaysAnswer: I forget whole hands now. Twenty years, I never forgot a card.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Nothing. Dry hands, steady as a surgeon. Always have been.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: No late nights since I quit cards. I sleep like a Party official.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Nothing. At forty-five a man paces himself. Rest, eat, no trouble.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
    cameraTrigger: 
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - You have a poker face that would bankrupt me in ten minutes.
    - The odds keep shifting. I keep adjusting. That's all you can do.
    midDays:
    - I found a four-leaf clover in the ash. Taking that as a sign.
    - The house always wins, does it not? Right now it's on fire.
    finalDays:
    - No out-bluffing the end of the world. Going home to fold.
    - Every player knows when to walk away. I'm almost there.
    uncannyEarlyDays: []
    uncannyMidDays: []
    uncannyFinalDays: []
  IDNumber: 3488018
